# chrysalis project manifest (#67 Phase 5c) — `spatio-flux` is a MIXED package: its
# OWN native crate (`sf_core()` / `sf_modules()` = the kinetics / diffusion / particle /
# FBA processes) plus its `.ys` modules under `ys/`. A `.ys` here runs via the codegen
# path: `chrysalis run` generates + builds + caches a runner that links this crate, then
# runs the program against `sf_core()` directly (surface = std ⊔ `sf_modules()`), no
# resolver. The crate exposes the `spatio_flux::prelude::{core, modules}` convention.
#
# Migrated from the legacy `package spatio-flux` directive to the structured `native:`
# field; both still work, but the structured manifest is the one codegen path going
# forward (the legacy directive retires once nothing — incl. out-of-repo projects — uses it).
def package = {
  name: 'spatio-flux',
  native: '.',
}
